{"name":"Cleopatra","hex":"#007590","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cleopatra","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A given name of women in the Ptolemaic dynasty of Egypt; notably Queen Cleopatra VII of Egypt (69–30 BCE); last of the Ptolemy line.","A female given name from Ancient Greek."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woman of great seductive beauty.","A variety of apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cleopatra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cleopatra","blocks":[{"text":"Cleopatra VII Thea Philopator was Queen of the Ptolemaic Kingdom of Egypt from 51 to 30 BC, and the last active Hellenistic pharaoh. A member of the Ptolemaic dynasty, she was a descendant of its founder, Ptolemy I Soter, a Macedonian Greek general and companion of Alexander the Great. Cleopatra's first language was Koine Greek, and she is the only Ptolemaic ruler known to have learned the Egyptian language, among several others. After her death, Egypt became a province of the Roman Empire, marking the end of the Hellenistic period, which had begun with the death of Alexander in 323 BC."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Kleopatra-VII.-Altes-Museum-Berlin1.jpg/330px-Kleopatra-VII.-Altes-Museum-Berlin1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra"},{"title":"Cleopatra (1963 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cleopatra is a 1963 American epic historical drama film directed by Joseph L. Mankiewicz, who co-wrote the screenplay with Ranald MacDougall and Sidney Buchman, adapted from the 1957 book The Life and Times of Cleopatra by Carlo Maria Franzero, and from histories by Plutarch, Suetonius, and Appian. The film stars Elizabeth Taylor in the eponymous role, along with Richard Burton, Rex Harrison, Roddy McDowall and Martin Landau. It chronicles the struggles of the young queen Cleopatra VII of Egypt to resist the imperial ambitions of Rome."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cleopatra_poster.jpg/330px-Cleopatra_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra_(1963_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg/500px-Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg/500px-Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACleopatra_signature_bw.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG/500px-Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG/1280px-Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG/500px-Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ptolemy_XII_Auletes_Louvre_Ma3449.jpg/500px-Ptolemy_XII_Auletes_Louvre_Ma3449.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thu